WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.812
JAMIE: According to AP, Meta Ray-Ban
glasses alone have sold more than seven

00:00:03.812 --> 00:00:07.625
JAMIE: million units. Seven million. And
right now there is no California law

00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:11.437
JAMIE: requiring those glasses to signal
anything when they're capturing you.
That's the

00:00:11.437 --> 00:00:15.249
JAMIE: gap the bill was trying to close.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.450
ALEX: And Newsom said no because—

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:20.804
RUFUS: The definition of "wearable
recording device" was too broad. His
specific objection

00:00:20.804 --> 00:00:24.132
RUFUS: was that the bill's language
would have swept in devices its authors

00:00:24.132 --> 00:00:27.461
RUFUS: probably didn't intend to cover.

00:00:27.571 --> 00:00:31.691
JAMIE: Which might be true. But "too
broad" is a reason to rewrite

00:00:31.691 --> 00:00:35.811
JAMIE: the bill, not kill it entirely.
Those are two different problems.
